    "note": "House Draft 1. Covers electric guns (stun-type devices), not firearms; counted as gun policy because it sits in the firearms chapter. Section 3 adds the new section to the HRS 134-87 exemption for law enforcement and National Guard. Amendments after HD1 are not in the text read."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): It shall be unlawful for any person to intentionally, knowingly, or recklessly carry or possess an electric gun, whether operational or not, on the following locations and premises:\nSECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): (1) A public school, as defined by section 302A-101, which includes but is not limited to any building, grounds, facility, structure, and appurtenant parking structure or lot;\nSECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): (4) An airport, as defined by section 261-1, which includes any terminal, building, structure, facility, and appurtenant parking structure or lot;\nSECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): (5) A public mass transit vehicle;\nSECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): (c) The presence of a person at any location or premises in subsection (a) shall be prima facie evidence that the person knows it is such a location or premises.\nSECTION 2 (new, HRS ch. 134 part V): (d) Any person violating this section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor."
}